WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.803
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:04.803
I appreciate it.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.005
I want to welcome
Damon and Stro.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.340
Welcome back, guys!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.608
Nice to see you guys again.
-Yay!

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.411
-We missed you.
Alright, get ready for --

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.213
You better really laugh it up
for these jokes.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.381
Here we go.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:18.918
You are now the audience,
as well as the band.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.587
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.222
Well, guys, as coronavirus cases
keep going up

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:26.026
and President Trump's approval
rating keeps going down,

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.327
he's decided
to bring back something

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.327
we haven't seen in a while.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:29.562
Check it out.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.398
-Three months later,
unable to hold his rallies

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.934
and floundering in the polls,
President Trump

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:39.172
announces that
televised briefings are back.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.740
-That's right --
today was Trump's

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.709
first coronavirus briefing
in almost three months

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.511
or, as that's known
in Trump time,

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.014
about 82 tell-all books.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.116
The briefing got off
to a rough start

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.219
when Trump asked the press,
"Okay, what did I miss?"

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.088
"Too much."

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:58.157
I'm going to say it once more --
three months.

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.727
Yeah, usually when someone
disappears for three months,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:04.096
they end up on their own episode
of "Unsolved Mysteries."

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:06.599
That's right --
Trump's briefings are back.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.968
Really? This is like
Samsung bringing back

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:13.539
their exploding Galaxy phone.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.441
The press secretary
also said the briefings

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.444
will focus on Trump's
accomplishments on the virus.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.580
So at least they'll be short.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.881
I'm excited
the briefings are back,

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.484
'cause I just want to see what
kind of treatments

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.485
Trump comes up with on the spot.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:30.723
[ As Trump ] Have we tried
canceling the virus?

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.991
Can we get it
canceled on Twitter?

00:01:32.991 --> 00:01:37.864
#CoronavirusOverParty?

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.165
[ Normal voice ] There was
actually a fun moment

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.933
during the briefing
when a reporter yelled,

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:44.804
"Hey, it's Chris Wallace,"
and Trump dove under the podium.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.839
But while Trump is holding
coronavirus briefings,

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.441
Dr. Fauci will spend the week

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.277
preparing for his
next big public appearance.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.112 line:0%
-The Washington Nationals
have just announced

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:55.681 line:0%
that Dr. Anthony Fauci,
a great Nats fan,

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:58.150 line:0%
will throw out the
ceremonial first pitch

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:01.387 line:0%
on opening day this Thursday,
against the New York Yankees.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.289 line:0%
-First of all,
not to be a downer, CNN,

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:06.860 line:0%
but I'm not sure Dr. Fauci
throwing out a first pitch

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.229 line:0%
qualifies as breaking news.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.868
Dr. Fauci will throw out the
first pitch on Thursday.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.870
It's a great idea,
until he spends 20 minutes

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.605
rubbing his balls with Purell.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.507
[ Tuba plays ]

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.275
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:28.447
Welcome back.
Welcome back, Damon.

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:30.550
Fauci is a small man,
so he's going to wear

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:34.453
one of those tiny helmets
they serve ice cream in.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:37.957
[ Laughs ]

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.859
You know Trump
is jealous about this.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.394
But, look, if he wants to
stand in front

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:44.663
of thousands of empty seats,
he could just go back to Tulsa.

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:47.833
-Ooh!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:50.136
-Yeah, as sports
begin to return,

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.138
it's still not safe
for fans to be in attendance.

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:54.873
Well, a Pittsburgh area company

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:56.609
said they developed
something that might help.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.677
Watch this.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.712 line:0%
-Aeras Fog Company developed
a drone

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.782 line:0%
with enough power
to sanitize entire stadiums

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:06.586 line:0%
in three hours using
electrostatic technology.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:09.188
-Which is great,
until 10 minutes later,

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.724
when a bunch of fans carrying
the virus show up for the game.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:18.397
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:19.665
The company was like, "Relax.

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.500
All we're going to do is fly
a giant robot around

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.668
while we drop chemicals
from the sky.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.703
What's the big deal?

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:29.809
What's the big 'D'?"

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.044
That's right -- we've gone from
Air Force flyovers

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:35.248
to a guy operating a drone
from a lawn chair.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.116
Baseball fans were like,
keep that for next season

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:40.419
and just fill it with beer.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:43.389
Moving on, a new study by
the National Sleep Foundation

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:47.393
found 20% of Americans
sleep with their eyes open.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.929
20%. Tariq, isn't that crazy?

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:56.602
Yeah, I'm practically
speechless, too.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:04:01.541
Can you imagine sleeping
with your eyes open?

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.675
Tariq?

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.610
Hello?

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.979
-[ Snoring ]

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:09.148
-Is he snoring?

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.584
Can someone take off
his glasses?

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.620
-I'll try. Here.
♪♪

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.160
-Tariq, what's going on, bud?

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.529
-[ Snoring ]

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.732
-Tariq, are you...

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:28.534
I think he's sleeping
with his eyes open.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.770
-I don't know.
He must be one of them 20%.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.240
-Is there any way to see what
he's dreaming about?

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.441
Do we have that technology?

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.344
[ Harp plays ]

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.681
Hey, it's us hanging out
before social distancing.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:45.618
I can't be mad about that.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.386
-Aah!

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:48.854
-Tariq, what?

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:50.022
-Yeah, sorry about that, man.

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:53.158
I was just having a nightmare.

00:04:53.158 --> 00:04:56.462
-Tariq Trotter, everyone.
-Wait. Where are my glasses?

00:04:56.462 --> 00:05:00.633
♪♪

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:06.372
-Well, guys, some TV news.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.607
Yeah.

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:12.178
-One more.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:19.518
-Guys, some TV news.

00:05:19.518 --> 00:05:22.588
After being delayed for several
months because of COVID,

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.158
it looks like "The Bachelorette"
is coming back.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.092
-Clare Crawley
hasn't let a pandemic

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:28.795
get in the way of finding love.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.263
They're shooting in Palm Springs

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.931
at the La Quinta
Resort &amp; Club.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.033
The entire cast and crew
is quarantining

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.635
at the resort before shooting.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.603
-Don't worry.
They're being very careful.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.404
They don't get in
a hot tub together.

00:05:39.404 --> 00:05:44.877
They sit in two separate tubs
like a Cialis commercial.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:45.945
And this is good.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.679
Each episode
ends with Clare asking,

00:05:47.679 --> 00:05:50.950
"Will you accept
this nose swab?"

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.417
This is interesting, though,
actually, 'cause, usually,

00:05:52.417 --> 00:05:53.719
the Bachelorette and the winner

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:58.223
become socially distant
after the show, so...

00:05:58.223 --> 00:06:00.459
Meanwhile, at this very moment,
the Bachelor Mansion

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:05.731
is being hosed down by
the chemical drone, so...

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:08.667
Well, this is exciting.
Oh! I love this story.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.170
I saw that Cheez-Its
is bringing back its box

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.040
that's half house wine,
half Cheez-Its.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.041
It comes out on Thursday.
Take a look at this.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.176
That's right!

00:06:18.176 --> 00:06:20.313
Boxed wine and Cheez-Its,

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.248
the official breakfast
of quarantine.

00:06:23.248 --> 00:06:24.717
Nowadays,
Americans are thinking,

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.885
"I need something stronger.

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:29.555
You got Flamin' Hot Doritos
and absinthe?"

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:33.592
It's a good thing to buy at
the self-checkout machine

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:36.396
so you don't have to make
eye contact with the cashier.

